    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d327">

                <pb facs="0391" n="341" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg341"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Mr. Smythe.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-03-21"><hi rendition="#italic">March 21,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 39.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am in receipt of your No. 51, of the 8th
                    instant, reporting the sale of the steam yacht <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Natalie</hi>, and requesting instructions in connection therewith.</p>
                <pb facs="0392" n="342" xml:id="pg342"/>
                <p>The bill of sale having been sent to the Treasury, no instructions in respect to
                    the transaction seem at present necessary.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin F. Uhl</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
